$MDESC::Type = "CTF_HamstersMaps";
$MDESC::Text = "<s3><f1>Mission Type: <f0> Capture the Flag" @
         "\n<f1>Author: <f0> Hamster_of_Doom!" @
	 "\n<f1>Questions, Comments, Pity: <f0> rvr279@home.com" @
 	 "\n<f1>ICQ: <f0> 25400277 <f1>AIM: <f0> Rover v1" @	 
	 "\n<f1>Map Version: <f0> 1.3" @
	 "\n<f1>Updates: <f0> http://members.home.net/rvr279/hamsterr" @
	 "\n<f1>Map Type: <f0> Server-Side" @
	 "\n<f1>Planet: <f0> Darius" @
         "\n<f1>System: <f0> Gaiden" @
         "\n<f1>Gravity: <f0> Normal" @ 
	 "\n<f1>Weather: <f0> Foggy" @
         "\n<f1>Time of Day: <f0> Midday" @ 
         "\n<f1>Date: <f0> January 15th, 4083" @
         "\n<f1>Campaign: <f0> Grid Iron" @         
	 "\n<f1># of Captures to Victory: <f0> 15" @
	 "\n<f1># of Teams: <f0> 2" @
	 "\n<f1>Max # of Players: <f0> 16" @
         "\n\n<f1>Briefing:<f0> Listen up soldiers! We have entered the glorious Tournament of the Crimson Son to prove our valor and gain control of the Larus region. This is the prize that the Freedom Corp. is offering to its winner! The Larus system is a rich economic hub and could provide us with everything we need to finish our enemy. Unfortunately, they know this and have entered the tournament as well. Soldiers, I don't need to remind you that this is no mere game. This is a battle to the death! So get out there and humiliate our enemies!\n\nFailure is not an option.\n\nDISMISSED!\n\n<f1>Tips:\n<f0>There are three switches to control. These switches provide only point bonuses, but that is an understatement.\nMinimal defenses exist on this level. Make sure to relegate teammates to defense.\nThere are no exposed generators.\nThe ammo stations in the left and right wings can be used by either team.\nUse the landscape to your advantage, but watch out! The enemy can do the same.\nKeep your eyes open for enemies that don't take the direct path into your base!\n\n<f1>Version History<f0>\nVers. 1.3\nProvided power to command station in side wing of arena.\n\nVers 1.2\nUpdated contact info.\n\nVers. 1.1\nLowered a floating crate to the ground.\nAdded beacons and mortar ammo on the ground for pick ups.\n\n<f1>Thanks to:\n<f0>Shadow of Death and Tedaw for debuting my maps on their server!\nOmnipotent & others for their mapping tutorials.\nThe mapping community at large for inspiration, demonstration, and perspiration.\nAnd of course the team at Dynamix for Tribes!";

